<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  M9b: the D-pad flag keyed on the DEVICE, not on the orientation.

  Every other bool here is a layout question, and for those `-port` is exactly right: a phone
  browses in portrait. But "does this device drive the UI with a D-pad?" is not an orientation
  question, and the player is where that bites — a fullscreen video player is LANDSCAPE on a
  phone too, so it resolved to the `values/` (TV) answer and the touch gesture layer was never
  attached. That is why the handset reported Live still had no tap and no zapping after M9.

  `-television` is Android's own uiMode qualifier: a Fire TV / Google TV always matches it, a
  phone never does, in any orientation. So TV keeps the D-pad model everywhere, and a phone gets
  the touch model everywhere — including fullscreen playback.
-->
<resources>
    <bool name="ui_uses_dpad_focus">true</bool>
    <!-- Same reasoning: a row taking focus from a touch is a TV behaviour, not a portrait one. -->
    <bool name="rows_focusable_in_touch_mode">true</bool>
</resources>
